      "side": 1,
      "message": "Do you expect the following \"history\" is used for forwarded number, and it is notified to Dialer as TelephonyManagerCompat.EVENT_CALL_FORWARDED?\nhttps://android.googlesource.com/platform/frameworks/opt/telephony/+/master/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/gsm/SuppServiceNotification.java#39\nhttps://android.googlesource.com/platform/frameworks/base/+/master/telephony/java/android/telephony/ims/ImsSuppServiceNotification.java#47\n\nWe considered and discussed it with our Modem teams, but we think it\u0027s not recommended due to following two reasons.\n\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\n1) Radio hal interface of SuppSvcNotification does not support the \"history\". We need to add it newly.\nhttps://android.googlesource.com/platform/hardware/interfaces/+/master/radio/1.0/types.hal#1879\n\n2) Basically, the history(forwardedNumber) should be shown on InCallUI at the same time when receiving new MT call.\nIf we use separate notifications to receive incoming call(by UNSOL_RESPONSE_CALL_STATE_CHANGED and GET_CURRENT_CALLS) and forwarded number(by UNSOL_SUPP_SVC_NOTIFICATION), it might cause some \"time lag\".\n\nAnd for your reference, as far as we know, Qualcomm modem has never used(notified) UNSOL_SUPP_SVC_NOTIFICATION for both gsm/ims until now. Current Qualcomm modem includes the history info in Call Info to notify these information together.\n\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\nFrom above point of view, we\u0027d like to suggest to add this forwardedNumber in Call Info.",
